			"date": "2024-09-25T23:31:47.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> ah, a docs PR!</p><p>I'm not sure how you like to tackle that stuff, but I've come to discover it's so-o-o much easier to document new features in its own docs PR than co-located with code (Bridgetown’s a monorepo). I used to think I should try to write docs as if it's part of a checklist along with tests and other code-level concerns, and that really gunked up the works.</p><p>Anyways…just curious!</p>",
